        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x) = \\ln 2 + 2e^{x}$, find $f^{\u2032}(x)$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $ln\u20612$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nUsing the addition rule, then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln\u20612+2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln\u20612)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =0+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
